35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The badge records show we arrive at very different times, so the first-come spots are gone early.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The billing is by area, not heads. Empty desks still cost us 41,000 yen a month.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The sound is nine decibels higher by the printer. That is a real difference, not a feeling.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,The physio note says my current setup took days to settle. Moving it resets that process.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The survey says daylight was the biggest complaint, but the plan gives three desks the wall.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if empty desks cost money, we need to make sure the new layout is actually used.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, exactly. And every time we move a desk, facilities charge 6,200 yen to re-run the lines.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, if your setup takes days to settle, you should not be in the high-traffic row.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, I agree. The window side is quieter and my body is already calibrated for that spot.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, if we put the late arrivals near the window, the early ones get the wall.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I am worried that the ""quiet"" spots will be claimed by the early arrivals, leaving us with the noise.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The 6,200 yen per move is a strong argument for getting the layout right the first time.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"We need to assign the noisy row to people who do not need deep focus, or rotate it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,I will not rotate. My body needs consistency. The window side is the only logical choice for me.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,I think we should assign the window desks to the people who reported the most daylight complaints.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I will vote for the option that protects the morning gaps and gives the window to the late arrivals.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for the option that minimizes the number of desks we need to re-run power for.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,I will vote for the option that explicitly assigns the noisy row to the people who do not need silence.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,I will vote for the option that keeps my current window-side desk and documents the comfort requirement.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I will vote for the option that matches the survey's top complaint and gives the window to the late arrivals.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
